4.	The most common reasons for deportation are:
([DOT]a) criminal convictions;
(b) having become an inmate of an asylum or hospital for mental diseases, or having become a public charge in Canada;
Cc) illegal entry;
(d) failure to comply with medical or other regulations governing admission to Canada.
